ising Health Impact Assessment: the New Zealand experience</article-title><source>Impact Assessment and Project Appraisal</source><year>2008</year><volume>26</volume><fpage>2</fpage><lpage>16</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.3152/146155108X300547</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B54"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>Public Health Advisory Committee</collab></person-group><source>An idea whose time has come &#x02013; new opportunities for Health Impact Assessment in New Zealand public policy and planning</source><year>2007</year><publisher-name>Wellington, New Zealand: National Health Committee</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B55"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hay</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Kitcher</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>An analysis of the benefits of a cross-sectoral approach to a prospective Health Impact Assessment of a container port development</article-title><source>Environmental Impact Assessment Review</source><year>2004</year><volume>24</volume><fpage>199</fpage><lpage>206</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.eiar.2003.10.010</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B56"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Elliott</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Francis</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Making effective links to decision-making: key challenges for Health Impact Assessment</article-title><source>Environmental Impact Assessment Review</source><year>2005</year><volume>25</volume><fpage>747</fpage><lpage>757</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.eiar.2005.07.007</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B57"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Menzies</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name></